{
  "_note": "Which app, site or game is in front -> which tags. system_watcher.py reads this file; nothing here is code. Rename an exe and it works, add a game and it works.",
  "_shape": "apps and sites are lists of rules, checked top to bottom. A rule matches when ANY listed exe matches OR any title_regex matches, subject to exclude_exe / exclude_title_regex. A match adds ALL of its tags - that is how app_genshin and gaming arrive together.",
  "_flags": "require_title_regex -> the exe alone is not enough, the title must match too (generic hosts like javaw.exe). skip_browser -> do not fire on a browser tab that merely mentions the name. browser_only (sites) -> only match when the foreground exe is a listed browser.",
  "_emulators": "An emulator's exe alone only says 'an emulator' (tag: emulator). emulator_title_regex promotes it to the real game using the window title, which emulators normally set to the app name. Titles vary by emulator and by language, so check yours with --debug and add a pattern if it does not fire.",
  "_verify": "Exe names were taken from official installs and community documentation, and are treated as a starting set. If a game does not register, run the app, check what the window is actually called, and add it. 'osu!.exe' and 'Wuthering Waves.exe' are the ones most worth confirming yourself.",
  "_privacy": "Titles are matched in memory and discarded. Only the rule id, the display name and the tags below ever leave the watcher.",

